cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the measurements it produces, please cite both
  the software archive and the paper it accompanies.
title: >-
  vertebra-xray-core: identifiable three-dimensional Cobb angles from
  biplanar spine radiographs
abstract: >-
  A measurement core for spinal deformity. Four endplate corners per view
  constrain only two of the three rotations that define a vertebra's
  orientation, so a three-dimensional Cobb angle computed from biplanar
  endplate landmarks alone is not identifiable. Adding the two pedicle
  centroids, already visible on the frontal view, closes the system exactly.
  The package implements the measurement layer, a normative pedicle table, a
  training-free level assignment, per-case uncertainty, a CT path for ground
  truth, and licence-free phantoms with closed-form angles.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
